<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened runtime entitlements. Required for notarization, and every entry
  here is required by something this app actually does — a shorter list is a
  notarized build that launches and then cannot work.

  allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
    V8, and also the `claude` executable the Agent SDK bundles: it is a
    Bun-compiled single-file binary that unpacks and JITs at startup. It is
    signed as a nested binary with these same entitlements (see
    entitlementsInherit), so leaving them out breaks the CLI rather than the
    app, which is the harder failure to diagnose.

  disable-library-validation
    The SDK is asarUnpack'd and dynamically imported, node-pty is a native
    module, and the campus shim re-executes this app's own Electron binary
    with ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1. Library validation would refuse loads whose
    signing identity does not match the main executable's.

  allow-dyld-environment-variables
    Electron's own helper processes and the ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE path depend
    on environment the hardened runtime otherwise strips.

  Deliberately NOT here: the app sandbox. Agents run arbitrary commands in
  the user's own directories — that is the product — so a sandbox entitlement
  would either be a lie or a broken app.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
